area: model
case: 06-model-extremes
verification: explicit-divergence
oracle: python
projection: model
reason: pydantic holds a Python int of any width and FetchRequest.offset has no upper bound, so a 2**70 offset is accepted and re-encoded exactly; the port's FetchRequest.offset is an OCaml int, and the decoder accepts an Intlit only when it fits one, so it refuses 2**70 with 'outside the integer range'. Closing the gap needs a big-integer representation on the model surface — lib/server.ml and lib/engine.ml read offset as an int — so it is pinned as a platform limit and raised in the plan.
